The Gold discount implementation in the provided code (src/pricing/pricing.py) works as follows:

- It is part of the function calculate_discount which takes the subtotal amount and the customer tier.
- If the customer tier is "gold":
  - The base discount percent is set to 15%.
  - If the subtotal is greater than 1000, an additional 2% discount is added, making the total discount 17%.
  - The discount is then calculated as a fraction of the subtotal using the minimum of the discount percentage and 20 (which caps the discount percent at 20% just as a safeguard).
- The discount amount is returned as the subtotal multiplied by the discount fraction (discount_percent / 100).

